/* Termination of a terminating nested loop, after one unfolding of the outer
   loop into the query (the form the optimizer gives function_bubblesort of
   popl2023mod), with the bounds 10 lowered to 2:
int main() {
  int x1, x2;
  while (x1 <= 2) {
    x2 = 2;
    while (x2 > 1)
      x2 = x2 - 1;
    x1 = x1 + 1;
  }
  return 0;
}
   Valid.  The refuter's existential for x2' is nested in its existential for
   x1; once the refuter's x1 has two term alternatives, a strategy check that
   copies the clause per alternative without renaming the nested choice's
   result apart makes the refuter's check clause vacuous, and MuStrat answered
   invalid, with and without the optimizer's quantifier erasure. */
forall (d: int). Q d
s.t.
I (x1: int) (x2: int): bool =mu x1 > 2 \/ (forall (x2': int). negP x2 x2' \/ I (x1 + 1) x2') /\ J 2;
Q (d: int): bool =mu forall (x1: int) (x2: int). x1 > 2 \/ (forall (x2': int). negP x2 x2' \/ I (x1 + 1) x2') /\ J 2;
J (x2: int): bool =mu x2 <= 1 \/ J (x2 - 1);
negP (x2: int) (x2': int): bool =nu (x2 > 1 \/ x2 != x2') /\ (x2 <= 1 \/ negP (x2 - 1) x2');
